post_install() {
  cat << 'EOF'
==> TAPE 16 has been installed.

Main command:
    tape16

The official Linux build is X11-backed. On a Wayland session it runs
through XWayland. The launcher sources:
    /usr/share/tape16/profiles/wayland.env   (Wayland login)
    /usr/share/tape16/profiles/x11.env       (X11 login)

Command-line tools:
    tape16-plugin-doctor
        Internal plugin diagnostic helper.
        Logs: ~/.config/TapeDAW/

    tape16-reset-defaults
        Reset UI/workflow preferences (timestamped backup).
        Does not remove licenses, sessions, recordings or plugins.
        Optional: tape16-reset-defaults --include-plugin-cache

    In the app UI, similar actions are in Plugin Manager:
        Deep Rescan, UNSCAN, Reset Plugin System

Audio:
    TAPE 16 talks JACK (libjack).
    Recommended: PipeWire + pipewire-jack + wireplumber
    Alternative: jack2
    Set the device and buffer in TAPE 16 Audio Settings.
    Optional: pacman -S realtime-privileges
              sudo usermod -aG realtime $USER
              then log out and back in

Wayland sessions:
    pacman -S xorg-xwayland
    
Optional launch flags:
    TAPE16_SURGE_EDITOR_MODE=isolated tape16
        Isolated Surge XT editor if the native window is blank.

    TAPE16_PREFER_NATIVE_WAYLAND=1 tape16
        Experimental. Not recommended by upstream.
        
Remote:
    Enabled by default on the local network (TAPE16_REMOTE_LAN=1).
    Disable with: TAPE16_REMOTE_LAN=0 tape16

    The QR code encodes http://IP:PORT/remote/#token=...
    If that IP is wrong (VPN, VM bridge, etc.), open the URL and
    replace the IP with this machine's address on the same network
    as your phone.

    Do not enable this on public or untrusted Wi-Fi.
    
More info:
    https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/PipeWire
    https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Realtime_process_management
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}
